  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "## Changes since 3.1.2\n\n### CliInvoke\n\n#### Fixed\n- Resource-policy setters no longer fail the launch when the child process exits first.\n- `OnStarted` always resumes the child process. It resumes a child process whose `HasExited` is already true, and it resumes threads through the process handle it holds instead of looking the process up by ID, which skips processes that are terminating.\n- The resume-failure handler in `OnStarted` catches `InvalidOperationException` and `Win32Exception` instead of `Exception`. Any other failure in the resume path now reaches the caller instead of causing a process kill and a rethrow.\n\n### CliInvoke.Specializations\n* Updated to use CliInvoke 3.1.3",
